}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

where \code{m = log(2 * D)}, \code{u1 = rho * cos(2 * theta)},
\code{u2 = rho * sin(2 * theta)} and \code{rho = log(aniso) / 2}. \code{V} then has
eigenvalues \verb{exp(m +/- rho)}, so the ratio of its axes is \code{aniso} and its
major axis lies at \code{theta}.

